# The build context is the repo root, and the repo root contains 691 MB of live runtime
# state. Without this file every `docker build` uploads the catalogue, the 255 MB spend
# ledger and every dossier to the daemon before the first instruction runs — and worse,
# `COPY . /app` would bake a point-in-time copy of the store INTO the image, where it
# would shadow the volume mount for anything that resolved a path before the mount.
#
# The store is state. It arrives on the volume, never in the image.
store/
storage/
signals/pending/
graphify-out/

# Build outputs and dependency trees. The image installs its own.
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/bin/
**/obj/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local-only. `.env` in particular must never be baked in: secrets reach the container
# through `fly secrets` or compose's env_file, both of which keep them out of the image
# layers and out of anything that can be pulled.
.env
.env.*
.git/
.claude/
.lux/keys/
*.log

# .github/ used to be excluded here, on the same "not needed at runtime" grounds as docs/.
# It is needed at runtime. scripts/deploy_status.py:55 resolves `ROOT / ".github/workflows"`
# and reads each deploy workflow's `paths:` filter to work out what a service is running and
# how far behind main it is; the console's /deploys tab is that function's output. Measured on
# prospector-engine 2026-08-20:
#
#     $ ls /app/.github/workflows
#     ls: cannot access '/app/.github/workflows': No such file or directory
#
# so every deployable rendered `state: UNKNOWN` with the reason ".github/workflows/deploy-web.yml
# is gone — this table names a workflow that does not exist". The workflows were never gone. The
# founder read the page as the deploy buttons not existing.
#
# It is 256 KB: 15 workflow files and 2 scripts, no secrets and no state.

# docs/ and specs/ used to be excluded here, on the grounds that documentation is not needed
# at runtime. That stopped being true on 2026-08-19, when the console gained a Docs tab and a
# Share tab that both read the repo's own markdown. Measured on prospector-engine 2026-08-20:
# `python -m prospector.ops.console_api read docs` returned count 0 with the note "there is no
# docs/ directory in this checkout", and the tab rendered that as an empty screen. The founder
# clicked it and reported that nothing happened.
#
# The screenshots still do not travel, but the text beside them now does. Excluding all of
# docs/design/ was too wide: measured 2026-08-21, it held 43 PNGs (21.5 MB) AND 25 text
# documents (1.1 MB of html, md, json and css) that prospector.ops.docs_view.docs_index
# lists. Those 25 were listed by the console and absent from the image, so the founder got a
# row that opened onto nothing. The PNGs all sit in these two directories and no console read
# view opens them, so naming the directories ships the text and leaves the images behind.
#
# Name DIRECTORIES here, not a glob like docs/design/**/*.png. A plain prefix is the shape
# every matcher agrees on; mid-pattern ** is where Docker and the guard below can differ.
# If a new PNG directory appears under docs/design/, add it as its own line.
#
# tests/unit/test_the_image_ships_what_the_console_serves.py fails if a path a console read
# view resolves under is excluded again.
docs/design/diff/
docs/design/visual/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
